{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Artificial Moral Agent.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Artificial Moral Agent.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"artificial moral agent artificial moral agent","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Artificial Moral Agent.md","fileName":"Artificial Moral Agent.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Artificial Moral Agent","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 23:09\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Machine Moral Status]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Machine Moral Status","Functional Morality","Machine Moral Agency","aiethics.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Artificial Moral Agent.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Artificial Moral Agent.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"artificial moral agent artificial moral agent","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Artificial Moral Agent.md","fileName":"Artificial Moral Agent.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Artificial Moral Agent","heading":"Artificial Moral Agent","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"An artificial moral agent is a machine designed to select actions using moral rules, values, or learned evaluations. The design ambition ranges from systems that obey safety constraints to machines expected to resolve conflicts among values.\n\nThe central difficulty is that human ethics is not always a complete set of explicit rules. Moral judgment is also embodied, socially embedded, and sensitive to context. An artificial system may therefore display [[Functional Morality]] without possessing full [[Machine Moral Agency]]. Keeping that distinction clear prevents engineered compliance from being mistaken for moral understanding or responsibility.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Machine Moral Status","Functional Morality","Machine Moral Agency","aiethics.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Artificial Moral Agent.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Artificial Moral Agent.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"artificial moral agent artificial moral agent","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Artificial Moral Agent.md","fileName":"Artificial Moral Agent.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Artificial Moral Agent","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[aiethics.epub]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Machine Moral Status","Functional Morality","Machine Moral Agency","aiethics.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}